WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.321
Every live biotherapeutic starts with the same gamble:

00:00:06.321 --> 00:00:08.554
a peptide designed by guesswork.

00:00:08.554 --> 00:00:11.057
Cozy Peptide replaces the guesswork.

00:00:11.057 --> 00:00:15.996
Name the disease — get a novel AI-designed peptide, screened for safety,

00:00:15.996 --> 00:00:20.528
compiled to DNA, ready for engineered bacteria to produce locally.

00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:23.370
No pharma factory, no ten-year pipeline —

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.820
just a designed DNA order and a bacterial chassis.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.850
Watch one get designed, live.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.207
Start with a real target: C.

00:00:31.207 --> 00:00:32.981
difficile gut infection.

00:00:32.981 --> 00:00:37.237
One click selects it — the designer picks the best scaffold

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:42.203
and bacterial factory for this target: a hairpin peptide brewed in E.

00:00:42.203 --> 00:00:43.125
coli Nissle.

00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:46.712
Meta AI reads the literature, drafts candidates,

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:51.475
then revises them against safety, chassis, and biocontainment checks —

00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:53.621
every step streaming on screen.

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:57.982
Watch the status feed: literature grounding, candidate drafting,

00:00:57.982 --> 00:01:02.275
verification, chassis matching — each check logged in the feed.

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:06.747
Out comes a verified peptide sequence with its DNA order,

00:01:06.747 --> 00:01:10.344
a CRO-ready lab handoff, and a full audit ledger.

00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:14.589
Every AI choice is cited there — literature, safety audit,

00:01:14.589 --> 00:01:16.675
and chassis checks included.

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:19.049
And the guardrails are real.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.410
Ask for a toxin and the same server-side blocklist refuses —

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.698
try it live, right on the page.

00:01:25.698 --> 00:01:30.846
No toxins, no pathogens, no synthesis protocols for flagged sequences —

00:01:30.846 --> 00:01:31.275
ever.

00:01:31.575 --> 00:01:33.085
Then the loop closes.

00:01:33.085 --> 00:01:36.928
The Lab Guide walks any wet lab from DNA order to assay

00:01:36.928 --> 00:01:41.114
results — or preview the whole thing with zero setup in demo

00:01:41.114 --> 00:01:45.575
mode, from DNA order to assay results that feed the next design.

00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:49.879
Even microscopy gets AI: one click segments colony images

00:01:49.879 --> 00:01:52.847
and files the analysis to the run ledger —

00:01:52.847 --> 00:01:56.575
microscopy verified before you pay for the next loop.
